messages:
Carla: Quick a11y sanity check on the latest perf dashboard mock: https://design.redwood/perf/compact-v4. Main flags from support: muted numbers hard to read, filter search skip, and screen reader noise on frequent metric updates. Any quick wins?

Ben: Ran a fast axe pass. Primary issue: muted labels use #6D6D6D on #FFFFFF -> ~3.9:1. Suggest updating token `--text-muted` to a darker hex. Focus ring: currently a subtle inset shadow that disappears on some platforms, recommend an outline approach.

Irene: On SR patterns: avoid many aria-live regions for frequent metric updates; that gets noisy. Use a single offscreen `aria-live="polite"` status element for global messages and only update it when content meaningfully changes. For cards: if they are navigational landmarks use `role=region` + `aria-labelledby`; if they are a loose list use `role=group` so SR users don't get extra landmarks.

A11yBot: automated-scan: issues=8; color-contrast(2), focus-visible(1), skip-link(1), aria-roles(2), DOM-order(2). full report: https://a11y.redwood/reports/1782504444.json :mag:

Carla: Quick implementation plan: 1) update color tokens; 2) add skip link and ensure `main#content` receives programmatic focus on route transitions; 3) fix filter chip DOM order; 4) consolidate live regions.

Ben: Token proposals: `--text-muted: #2E2E2E` (meets 4.5+ on white), `--focus-ring: #0055CC`. Focus CSS snippet: ```css
.skip-link { position: absolute; left: -999px; }
.skip-link:focus { left: 16px; top: 8px; }
:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid var(--focus-ring); outline-offset: 2px; }
```

Irene: Route focus JS example (avoid double announcements): ```js
// after SPA route change
document.title = newTitle;
const main = document.getElementById('content');
if (main) {
  main.setAttribute('tabindex','-1');
  main.focus();
  main.removeAttribute('tabindex');
}
// do NOT call announceViaLive(newTitle) here to avoid duplicate SR output
```

Ben: For filter chips: do NOT use CSS `order` to change tab order. Keep DOM order consistent with visual order. If responsive layout requires visual reorder, sync tabindex or use roving tabindex pattern.

Irene: Virtualized list notes: emit `aria-posinset` and `aria-setsize`, and include stable `data-model-id` attributes. For value readout use descriptive aria-labels e.g. `aria-label="Latency 95th percentile, 120 milliseconds"`. Decorative sparklines should have `aria-hidden="true"`.

QA: I'll add CI contrast checks and keyboard smoke tests: tab through skip link -> nav -> filters -> first card. Manual acceptance: NVDA + VoiceOver quick pass and confirm no double announcements on nav. Acceptance criteria: body text >=4.5:1, visible keyboard outline, skip link works, cards have aria-labelledby/role, virtual list exposes posinset/setsize.

Maya: Prioritization: patch release. Owners: Ben -> tokens + focus styles + DOM order fixes; Irene -> SR copy + virtualized list attrs; QA -> tests. Target PR by 1783100000 (end of sprint).

Carla: Thanks everyone :thumbsup: Please attach screenshots and a small pairing session if any of the NVDA items look odd. Reopen thread if blocked.
